-- title:
--   Hurewicz map is surjective on a reduced CW model (r-cell generators)
-- statement:
--   The Hurewicz map is surjective: $r$-cells generate both sides.
--
--   Let $r=n+2$ and let $Y$ be a reduced CW model in degree $r$ with $H_i(Y;\mathbb{Z})=0$ for all $0<i<r$.  Then the Hurewicz homomorphism $h:\pi_r(Y,y)\to H_r(Y;\mathbb{Z})$ is surjective.
--
--   Since all cells of degree $<r$ are collapsed, the cellular chain group $C_r$ is generated by the $r$-cells and $H_r(Y)=C_r/\partial C_{r+1}$ is generated by their classes.  Each $r$-cell is attached by a based sphere $S^r\to Y$, and the image of its homotopy class under $h$ is exactly the singular homology class of that cell.  Hence every generator of $H_r$ is hit by $h$.  Equivalently this is the spherical realization of homology generators — the content of the platform theorem `PoincareFormalization.exists_map_sphere_homology_isIso`.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The statement takes the Hurewicz map $h$ as an explicit additive homomorphism argument and concludes `Function.Surjective h`, so it composes with the existence child and the injectivity child by `AddEquiv.ofBijective`.
-- source:
--   A. Hatcher, Algebraic Topology, Cambridge University Press (2002), §4.2 Theorem 4.32 (Hurewicz) p. 366 and Proposition 4.13 (cellular approximation) p. 353; and https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/2063085365225863035 (the three-step proof sketch followed here).

import Mathlib.Topology.Homotopy.HomotopyGroup
import Mathlib.Topology.Category.TopCat.Basic
import Definitions.Def_HurewiczSketchV2
import Definitions.Def_SP4Homology

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace HurewiczSketchV2

/-- The Hurewicz map is surjective: `r`-cells generate both sides.

Let `r = n+2` and let `Y` be a reduced CW model in degree `r` whose homology vanishes
in degrees `0 < i < r`.  Then every class in `H_r(Y;ℤ)` lies in the image of the
Hurewicz homomorphism `h : π_r(Y,y) → H_r(Y;ℤ)`.

This is the "generators" half of the cellular comparison in the Hurewicz proof.  Since
the low cells of `Y` are collapsed, `H_r` is generated by the `r`-cells; each `r`-cell
is a based sphere `S^r → Y`, and its image under `h` is the corresponding singular
homology class.  Equivalently, every homology generator is realized by a map from a
sphere — the content of the platform theorem
`PoincareFormalization.exists_map_sphere_homology_isIso`. -/
theorem hurewicz_surjective_of_reduced_cw (n : ℕ) (Y : TopCat) (y : Y)
    (hY : ReducedCWModel (n + 2) Y)
    (hH : ∀ i : ℕ, 0 < i → i < n + 2 → CategoryTheory.Limits.IsZero (SP4Homology.H i Y))
    (h : Additive (HomotopyGroup.Pi (n + 2) Y y) →+ SP4Homology.H (n + 2) Y) :
    Function.Surjective h := by
  sorry

end HurewiczSketchV2
